From 174cea12fb4f6388f0bf288bba1aec8f313450b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 00:32:01 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 0043-vela-vk-defer core: bookkeeping of the deferred Vulkan
 upscale, free of Vulkan headers (hooks/VelaVkDeferCore.h): Tracker = what the
 hooks saw of the game's command buffers (begun, secondary, inside a render
 pass, queue family of the pool) and which recorded jobs wait for a command
 buffer to reach vkQueueSubmit (a job on a secondary follows
 vkCmdExecuteCommands to the primary; a re-begun / reset / freed buffer loses
 its jobs); Ring = 4 own command buffers, strict round robin, Free ->
 Recording -> Ready -> InFlight, stale rule for the next-Evaluate path (a job
 no hook submits is due one Evaluate later, a hook job two later), drop by
 handle. Host-side test arm64ec/tests/vk_defer_core_test.cpp (not in the DLL):
 6058 checks

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
